WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.5 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Roles and role descriptions

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A role card shows the results expected and what each person can decide, founders included.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:24.800
A role card describes what a person contributes, the results expected and what they can decide. A task list alone does not say what success looks like.

4
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:25.800
What a role card holds

5
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:37.130
Purpose and results: Why the role exists and what success looks like by the end of the year. For example: Bakery sales lead: three cafés buying bread every week by December.

6
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:48.459
Responsibilities: The main areas of work the role owns, with one owner per area. For example: The youth club's activities lead owns the session plan and the volunteer rota.

7
00:00:48.459 --> 00:01:00.530
Decisions and limits: What the role can decide alone, its spending limits and when to escalate. For example: The tutoring coordinator buys materials within the monthly budget; anything more goes to both founders.

8
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:13.430
Links and support: Who the role works with and the support it needs to succeed. For example: The repair café's volunteer lead works with the host venue and has a monthly check-in.

9
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.430
Why they matter

10
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:20.474
1. Co-founder roles are the first to blur; writing them down prevents friction.

11
00:01:20.474 --> 00:01:25.778
2. People know what they can decide without asking every time.

12
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:32.081
3. One owner per area means nothing important falls between people.

13
00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:33.081
What they guide

14
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:38.015
1. Your first job adverts and contracts in Module 4.

15
00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:43.319
2. Your RACI and delegation of authority, later in this module.

16
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.252
3. Your check-ins: progress reviewed against each role's expected results.

17
00:01:49.652 --> 00:01:50.252
What to avoid

18
00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:55.556
Writing only a task list, with no results or authority.

19
00:01:55.556 --> 00:02:00.859
Shared ownership of an area, which usually means no ownership.

20
00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:06.793
Forgetting role cards for founders, volunteers and board officers.

21
00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.193
You write role cards for the founders and your first essential roles.

22
00:02:09.193 --> 00:02:13.193
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:17.793
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
